WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.720
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:12.240
Today we are going to play some more with OpenAI’s&nbsp;
amazing technique DALL-E 2, where we can write&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:19.440
a text description, and the AI creates an&nbsp;
amazing image of exactly that. That sounds cool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.680
and it gets even cooler the&nbsp;
crazier the ideas we give to it.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.640
This is an AI endowed with a diffusion-based&nbsp;
model, which means that when we ask it something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:36.800
it starts out from noise, and over&nbsp;
time, it iteratively refines this image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:43.440
to match our description better. And, over&nbsp;
time, magically, an absolutely incredible image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:50.960
emerges. This is a neural network that is given&nbsp;
a ton of images, and a piece of text description&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:57.760
that says what is in this image. That&nbsp;
is one image-caption pair. DALL-E 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:04.560
is given millions and millions of these pairs.&nbsp;
So, what can it do with all this knowledge?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:12.400
Well, the best part is that it can combine&nbsp;
things! Oh yes, this is the key. This does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:19.920
not copy images from this training data, but&nbsp;
it truly comes up with novel images. How?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.880
Well, after it had seen a&nbsp;
bunch of images of koalas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:32.560
and separately, a bunch of images of motorcycles,&nbsp;
it starts to understand the concept of both,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.920
and it will be able to combine the two&nbsp;
together into a completely new image.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:46.400
And here you can see how much DALL-E&nbsp;
2 has improved since DALL-E 1. It is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.680
on a completely different&nbsp;
level from its first iteration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:57.280
This is so much better, and once again,&nbsp;
this is an AI that was improved this much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:03.200
in just a year? I can hardly believe what&nbsp;
I am seeing here. What a time to be alive!

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.760
And now that some time has passed, new,&nbsp;
interesting capabilities have emerged.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.840
Now, hold on to your papers, and let’s&nbsp;
have a look at 10 more amazing examples.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:23.360
One, for instance, it can even create not&nbsp;
just images, but small videos. Videos?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:32.800
How? Well, look at this video where a victorian&nbsp;
house is getting modernized! Wow. So what is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:42.080
on here? Well, we can enter a text prompt, get an&nbsp;
image, then change the text just a tiny bit, get a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:49.120
slightly changed image, and repeat the process&nbsp;
over and over until we get an amazing video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:56.320
like this. We can also run this process backwards&nbsp;
and victorianize a modern building as well.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:02.160
Two, if you don’t believe that it can&nbsp;
combine several existing concepts into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.840
something that definitely does not exist, hold&nbsp;
on to your papers, and have a look at this one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.800
Oh yes, Apple products, Leonardo Da Vinci style.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:19.440
This is truly insane. If all this does not feel&nbsp;
like humanlike intelligence, I don’t know what is.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:26.080
Three, here is how the AI imagines&nbsp;
a robot learning a new language.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:35.440
Four, it can create new kinds of drinks, and,&nbsp;
my goodness. Well, I am super happy now. You are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:42.000
probably asking, Károly, why are you super happy?&nbsp;
Well, I am a light transport researcher by trade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:50.000
and I spend a great deal of my time computing&nbsp;
caustics. Oh yes, caustics are these beautiful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:56.720
patterns that emerge when we hit a reflective&nbsp;
or refractive object with light just the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:02.720
